// Title: Visual Studio Code Tunnel Remote File Creation
// Sigma ID: 56e05d41-ce99-4ecd-912d-93f019ee0b71
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-10-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control
// Description: Detects the creation of file by the "node.exe" process in the ".vscode-server" directory. Could
//   be a sign of remote file creation via VsCode tunnel feature
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_vscode_tunnel_remote_creation_artefacts.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\servers\\Stable-" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\server\\node.exe" and FolderPath contains "\\.vscode-server\\data\\User\\History\\"
